    "turn_text": "Well, it would solve the problem. One of the main things that's in it is reinstating the remain in Mexico policy, which was great under Trump. It automatically reduced the number of migrants that wanted to cross the border because what happens before the Trump policy and after now the Trump policy is people just cross over the border. They claim asylum. Once they claim asylum, they're in the country and they just wait for court hearing. Most of them don't show up with the remaining in Mexico policy. What happened is, yeah, you can claim asylum, but you have to wait in Mexico or another safe third country. Well, your claim is processed and you go to court. That makes sense to me. But of course, the Biden administration and the Democrats in the US Senate and the US House want open borders. I don't know exactly why they want open borders, but they prioritize illegal immigrants over US citizens.",
